---
/**
 * Section 02 — Dynamic regime change.
 *
 * Second of the five README arguments. Each of the three axes carries the
 * caveat the crate README states for it, because two of the three are
 * diagnostics rather than switches today, and a landing page that hides that
 * would be selling something the crate does not do.
 *
 * The log block is copied verbatim from the committed corridor run at
 * examples/avionics_examples/cfd/plasma_blackout/corridor/output.txt.
 */
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { rustDark, rustLight } from '../../../shiki-rust-themes.mjs';

const SHIKI = { light: rustLight, dark: rustDark };

const regime = `// RegimeClassify sits in the coupling stack and re-runs every step.
Coupling::between_steps()
    .then(FiniteRateIonizationStage::new(n_tot))   // writes "n_e"
    .then(RegimeClassify::new(l_char, trigger))    // reads it, classifies
    .build()

// field.regime() -> Option<RegimeClass<R>> {
//     model,            // Continuum | Slip | Transitional | FreeMolecular
//     knudsen,          // the Kn the model was selected from
//     plasma_frequency, // omega_p at the peak electron density
//     gnss_denied,      // omega_p above the configured comms band
//     mach_regime, thrust_state, touchdown,   // the powered-descent axes
// }

// A transition is a leg boundary: march until the classification changes.
let onset = CfdFlow::march(&nominal)
    .couple(world::corridor_coupling(1.0, 0))
    .from_field(world::initial_field())
    .until(|f, _| f.regime().map(|r| r.gnss_denied).unwrap_or(false))?;   // link lost

let exit = CfdFlow::march(&nominal)
    .alternate_context(&committed)
    .couple(world::corridor_coupling(1.0, 0))
    .from(peak.state())
    .until(|f, _| f.regime().map(|r| !r.gnss_denied).unwrap_or(false))?;  // link back`;

const regimeLog = `regime -> slip (GNSS-available), Kn=0.07829109848665225
regime -> slip (GNSS-denied), Kn=0.012690837165407727
regime -> continuum (GNSS-denied), Kn=0.00993838892165156
regime -> continuum (GNSS-available), Kn=0.0002551442196046344`;

const axes = [
  {
    name: 'Flow regime',
    on: 'freestream Knudsen number',
    body:
      'RegimeClassify bands the Knudsen number into a governing model: continuum Navier–Stokes, slip-corrected continuum, transitional, or free-molecular. Every transition is logged.',
    caveat:
      'Today this is a diagnostic carried on the evolved state. The crate does not switch closures on it, and no slip, transitional or free-molecular closure is implemented.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Dynamics regime',
    on: 'force ratio ε = a_aero/a_grav',
    body:
      'While gravity dominates, a trajectory advances on the exact KS-conformal core with aero applied as a between-step kick. Once aero dominates, direct Cowell integration is the accurate choice. This ratio is the criterion for entering and leaving orbit.',
    caveat:
      'RegimeSwitch and aero_gravity_ratio are public API, but the shipped navigation engine does not call them. Applying the switch is the caller’s job.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Link regime',
    on: 'evolved electron density',
    body:
      'The electron density sets the plasma frequency, and the plasma frequency decides whether the GNSS link exists. The Kalman filter’s measurement gating follows it.',
    caveat: null,
  },
];
---
<section class="cfd-sec page" data-rise>
  <header class="sec-head">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-coord">
      <span class="ix">02 / 07</span><span class="lb">Dynamic Regime Change</span>
    </p>
    <h2>Dynamic Regime Change</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      The regime is classified from the evolved state at every step. Nothing
      schedules it in advance, and the governing regime switches on the
      physics.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="panel corner-brackets body-panel rise">
    <p class="body">
      A vehicle entering or leaving orbit crosses several regimes on the way,
      and they do not change together. Three axes are tracked independently.
    </p>

    <dl class="axes">
      {axes.map((a) => (
        <div class="axis">
          <dt>{a.name} <span class="axis-on">on {a.on}</span></dt>
          <dd>
            {a.body}
            {a.caveat && <span class="caveat">{a.caveat}</span>}
          </dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <p class="body">
      The classifier is a stage in the coupling stack. It re-runs each step and
      writes its result onto the evolved field, and a march predicate reads it
      back. A transition is therefore an event the run finds, not a station it
      was told to stop at:
    </p>

    <Code code={regime} lang="rust" themes={SHIKI} />

    <p class="body">
      Blackout becomes an interval the run discovers. March to the onset event,
      fly the committed world through the dark, continue to the recovery event.
      Every transition lands in the provenance log. From a committed corridor
      run:
    </p>

    <Code code={regimeLog} lang="text" themes={SHIKI} />

    <p class="body">
      One descent moves through orbit-like dynamics, slip flow, continuum flow,
      comms blackout and reacquisition, in one uninterrupted program.
    </p>

    <p class="more">
      <a href="/tutorial/stage-1-corridor/">Walk 1: the classifier in the stack</a>
      <a href="/blueprints/handle-regime-change/">Blueprint: handle a regime change</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cfd-sec { max-width: var(--w-panel); }
  .sec-head { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .sec-head h2 { margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-3); }
  .lede { color: var(--fg-1); max-width: var(--measure-lede); margin: 0; }

  .body-panel { padding: var(--space-5); }
  .body { color: var(--fg-1); font-size: var(--t-body-sm); max-width: var(--measure); margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); }

  .axes { margin: 0 0 var(--space-5); display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); }
  .axis { padding-left: var(--space-4); border-left: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
  .axis dt { color: var(--fg-0); font-size: var(--t-body-sm); margin-bottom: var(--space-1); }
  .axis-on {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-eyebrow);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-eyebrow);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-2);
    margin-left: var(--space-2);
  }
  .axis dd { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-1); font-size: var(--t-body-sm); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .caveat { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--fg-2); }

  .more {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-1);
    font-size: var(--t-body-sm);
  }
</style>
